                <pb facs="0072" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg66"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of Imperial decree.</hi></head>
                <p>On the 27th of December, 1900, the following decree was issued:</p>
                <p>“We have duly perused Prince Ching’s and Li Hung-chang’s telegram, and it
                    behooves us to agree to the whole of the twelve articles.”</p>
                <p>[Seal of the Emperor.]</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="chinese-era gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-14"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuang Hsü</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">26th year, 11th month, 24th day</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 14,
                    1901</hi>)</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
